# Image placeholders — strict rule

**Photography stays grey placeholder boxes.** This covers hero photos, split images, card thumbnails and
before/after pictures. The client will supply real photos in a separate pass.

## Client-supplied brand assets — USE THESE (already delivered)

Logos, icons, OEM and review-platform logos are real assets in `public/`. Use them, not grey boxes.
Exactly one file per asset (the desktop export); resize with CSS for mobile — never keep a second mobile copy.

| Asset | Path | Use via |
|---|---|---|
| Kuroda logo (horizontal / vertical, color / white) | `public/brand/logo-{horizontal,vertical}-{color,white}.png` | `<Logo layout variant>` |
| Icon set (28px blue, 24px light-blue on navy, etc.) | `public/icons/*.png` | `<BrandIcon name>` |
| OEM + I-CAR logos | `public/oem/*.png` | `CredentialLogos`, hero trust bar |
| CARWISE / Google / Yelp logos (white) | `public/ratings/*.png` | `RatingsBar` |

For photography, do **not** use `<Image>`, `<img>`, `<ArtDirectedImage>`, `<SanityImage>`, `background-image`, or
any asset URL until explicitly told to. Replace every image reference you encounter with a `<div
class="bg-section-grey …">`.

During the build phase, **never** import, download, or embed real images. Use a grey placeholder `<div>` instead.
Images are provided by the client in a separate asset pass.

## The Figma MCP image rule

When using the Figma MCP (`get_design_context`, `get_screenshot`, etc.) the server returns
`http://localhost:*` image URLs. These are **temporary, local-only, and must NEVER appear in any
source file, component, or page** — not even as a comment, an `src` attribute, a CSS `url()`, or a
default prop value.

```astro
<!-- ✅ CORRECT — grey box placeholder -->
<div
  class="w-full bg-section-grey"
  style="aspect-ratio: 16 / 9;"
  aria-hidden="true"
/>
<!-- TODO: replace with <Image> when asset is ready -->

<!-- ❌ WRONG — Figma MCP localhost URL in production code -->
<img src="http://localhost:3845/..." alt="hero" />

<!-- ❌ WRONG — real image import -->
<Image src={heroPhoto} alt="…" />
```

## How to handle every image in Figma

1. Note the frame's width × height to compute the correct `aspect-ratio`.
2. Note the corner radius and apply a matching `rounded-*` class.
3. Render the grey box — **do not reach for the Figma-provided localhost URL**.
4. Leave the `<!-- TODO: replace with <Image> -->` comment on the placeholder.

## Correct placeholder shapes

| Figma image type | Placeholder classes |
|---|---|
| Full-bleed hero photo | `w-full h-full absolute inset-0 bg-section-grey` |
| Side image in a split | `w-full bg-section-grey rounded-[Xpx]` + `style="aspect-ratio: W/H"` |
| Card thumbnail | `w-full bg-section-grey rounded-t-[Xpx]` + `style="aspect-ratio: 4/3"` |
| Icon / small asset | `w-12 h-12 bg-section-grey rounded-full` |

## Site-wide grey-box locations (Kuroda Autobody)

Every one of these must be a grey box until the client delivers assets:

| Location | File | What to grey-box |
|---|---|---|
| Homepage hero | `src/pages/index.astro` | Right-side photo (`left: 200px → right: 0`) |
| Audience pathway cards | `src/pages/index.astro` | Each card image |
| Banner / split image | `src/pages/index.astro` | `bannerImage` section |
| Interior page heroes | `PageHero.astro` | Right-side photo |
| Service / area split images | Content sections | Side image in each split |
| Card thumbnails | `BlogCard` | Card image |

## Do not

- Save or reference any `localhost:*` URL from the Figma MCP server
- Import a photo, illustration, or icon from `src/assets/images/` until the client provides the file
- Leave a Figma screenshot URL inside an `<img>` or `background-image`
- Use `<SanityImage>` or `<Image>` for any visual photography/illustration
- Use a real OG image from Figma as `<Image>` — OG images are generated separately
